    "introduction": "Antofagasta is a mining group centred on copper production in Chile, with operations including Los Pelambres and Centinela. Its mines sell copper in forms such as concentrates and cathodes and also recover by-products including gold and molybdenum. A transport business serves industrial customers in northern Chile. Revenue depends on output and commodity prices, while mine profitability reflects ore quality, processing efficiency and the cost of energy, water and labour. Expansion projects require long planning periods and substantial capital. Its concentration in copper provides exposure to demand from electricity networks, construction and manufacturing, with environmental permissions and water infrastructure particularly important to operations.",
